                  The Shadow's EdGe Die Roller V1.2 9/21/96
                                   For CNet
                                  By FishBone

                         
                                ***What is It?***
        This is a fairly Simple Die Rolling program for CNet 3.+.  It is
intended for use with OnLine RPG's, (i.e. AD&D), But could Be used anywhere
else you have the need.  

                               ***Installation***
        O.K, this is really simple.  Copy the "Dice" Directory To where ever
you want to run it From (i.e. PFiles/GFiles).  Then Load the Program DieRoll10
into a text editor and edit the following lines:

            dp='gfiles:dice/'   To where ever you put the dice directory
            maint='25'          The lowest access level allowed to edit the
                             Log. I chose to set it this way to give the sysop
                             more control as compared to letting anyone with
                             BBs Maintenance access the reset and edit  
                             features.

        That's it.  Add dieroll10 to your P/Gfiles as an arexx prog and your
all set!

                                   ***Usage***
        When you enter the program, the first prompt is "Would you like to 
muffle all prompts?"  Selecting YES  will change the users global Muffle 
settings, and they will be changed back when they exit of the program. 
Then you will be greeted by a Short ANSI Menu, (O.K. guys, I realize it's
 kinda Cheesy, but ANSI isn't really My Strong Point). Then Select R, V, or Q.  
        Selecting "R" will start The Die roller.  You choose the size of the
die you want to roll, and then how many times you'd like roll it.  That's it,
the result will automatically be recorded in the log.  You can then decide if 
you want to roll more dice, or quit back to the main menu.
        Selecting "V" will display the log of rolls.  There will be a list of
all the dice (depending on the # of Dice rolled) and a total for each roll.  If
the user is at or above the access group specified above in 'maint=X' then a
menu will appear at the end of the log allowing you to [E]dit, which allows
you to directly edit the log through your default editor, [C]lear, which
automatically resets the log, and [Q]uit which quits back to the main menu.
If the user is not of the Access level specified, he will be returned 
to the Main menu automatically.
        Selecting Q will exit the program.

                                ***NOTES***
	The roller will currently only allow you to roll 10 dice at a time, As 
I Felt this was sufficient.
	When Viewing the log, There is a slight pause in between rolls, as for
some reason it seems the more program has been disabled, and this seemed the
best way to fix it for now.  At any time while reading the log, you can hit
the space bar or Control-C to abort the rest of the log.
	Plans for the Future include  Fixing the More Problem, and a complete
online character editor is already Under way (for AD&D particuarily, Maybe
RPG's As well?)

